Constellation OS -- third-party components
==========================================

Everything in this repository that we wrote is GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE).
The items below are third-party and keep their own licenses.  They are
included because a bootable image needs them; none of them is relicensed
by us.

Firmware blobs
--------------
rootfs-770ed/lib/firmware/b43/*.fw
    Broadcom BCM43xx ucode/PCM/initvals, extracted from the Broadcom STA
    driver (broadcom-wl-5.100.138) with b43-fwcutter 021.
    Provenance and the exact extraction command: lib/firmware/b43/SOURCE.txt
    Redistributed for use with the in-kernel b43 driver.  Broadcom's binary
    licence applies; the files are unmodified.

rootfs-770ed/lib/firmware/agere_*.bin (shipped inside the built image)
    Agere/Lucent ORiNOCO (Hermes) firmware, from linux-firmware.
    Redistributable per the linux-firmware LICENCE.* files for these blobs.

regulatory.db / regulatory.db.p7s (shipped inside the built image)
    wireless-regdb by Luis R. Rodriguez and contributors.  ISC-style
    licence; the p7s is the kernel's signature of the same database.

Vendored / patched upstream code
--------------------------------
third_party/patches/
    Patches against upstream projects, distributed under the license of the
    project they patch (apk-tools: GPL-2.0).

kernel/configs/*, busybox/configs/*, and the build scripts
    Configuration fragments and build glue, written by us (GPL-3.0).  The
    source code they configure is downloaded at build time from
    kernel.org / busybox.net / musl.libc.org / x.org / GNU and keeps its
    own license.

    Upstream source archives are pinned by sha256 in scripts/fetch-sources.sh
    and in the individual scripts/build-*-770ed.sh helpers, so a build always
    fetches exactly the version this project was tested with.

Not in this repository
----------------------
The BasicLinux 3.5 LCARS flavor (scripts/build-lcars-770ed.sh) builds from
an upstream checkout of github.com/queenkjuul/basiclinux-lcars, which
contains Slackware 4.0 packages and its own docs.  Nothing from that tree is
vendored here; the script only points at a local clone via LCARS_SRC.

ccode-cli (scripts/build-ccode-770ed.sh) is built from the user's own
checkout of the ccode project and is not vendored here either.
